<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills fell to 10.121 percent from 10.136 percent at the previous auction on December 3.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: June 10, 1997 (June 3, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.121 percent (10.136)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 970.55 milion (991 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1.119 billion (1.108 billion)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 9.999-10.149 percent (9.999-10.174)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 9.999-10.400 percent (9.999-10.280)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 108 (146)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 131 (172)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
